Guard CLayoutManager::moveTarget against a target with no space.

Fixes a SEGV reproduced four times on this machine (2026-08-04 x2,
2026-09-16, 2026-09-23), always with the identical backtrace:

    CInputManager::onSwipeUpdate
      CTrackpadGestures::gestureUpdate
        CMoveTrackpadGesture::update
          Layout::CLayoutManager::moveTarget
            Layout::CSpace::moveTarget      <- SEGV at +0x15

MoveGesture.cpp already guards the window (`if (!m_window) return;`), and
the only moveTarget call in update() is the floating branch, so the null
is not the window but the target's space: calling through an empty
SP<CSpace> enters CSpace::moveTarget with `this == nullptr`, which faults
on the first member read (`m_algorithm`). A null `target` itself would
have faulted one frame earlier instead, in CLayoutManager::moveTarget.

How the space goes null, from the report that produced the last one: the
moved window was Zoom's screen-share annotation toolbar, which on Hyprland
lands as its own toplevel and was rapidly unmapping and remapping itself
-- it hides when the pointer reaches it, reappears once the pointer is no
longer over it, and loops. CMoveTrackpadGesture captures m_window in
begin() and holds it for the whole gesture, so a window torn down mid-swipe
leaves a live window handle whose target has been detached from its space
(assignToSpace(nullptr) in this same file). Non-null window, null space,
and update() runs on the next swipe event.

The same file already treats a null space as reachable and guards for it
in changeFloatingMode() and moveTargetInDirection(); this brings
moveTarget() in line with them. resizeTarget() and setTargetGeom() have
the same exposure via ResizeGesture.cpp and are deliberately left alone
here -- no crash has been observed through them.

--- a/src/layout/LayoutManager.cpp
+++ b/src/layout/LayoutManager.cpp
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@
 }
 
 void CLayoutManager::moveTarget(const Vector2D& Δ, SP<ITarget> target) {
-    if (!target->floating())
+    if (!target || !target->floating() || !target->space())
         return;
 
     target->space()->moveTarget(Δ, target);
